# Shell scripts and Terraform templates MUST keep LF endings.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout converts cloud-init.sh.tftpl to CRLF, and the
# next `terraform apply` rewrites the launch template's user_data with \r\n. The
# script starts `#!/bin/bash`, so a trailing \r makes the kernel look for the
# interpreter "/bin/bash\r" and the runner never boots. Found 2026-08-28 while
# planning a one-line desired_capacity change: the plan wanted to rewrite 150
# lines of user_data purely because of line endings.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.tftpl   text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf
